Refactored the codebase around clearer responsibilities by replacing the procedural single-class design with a small graph model and a dedicated SCC solver in [StronglyConnectedComponents.java](/Users/allenjiang/Documents/ACE-Sycophancy-Codebase-Dataset/_worktrees/030_strongly_connected_components/StronglyConnectedComponents.java:1). The entrypoint is now just demo/output wiring, `DirectedGraph` owns graph construction, reversal, and vertex validation, and `KosarajuStronglyConnectedComponents` owns the algorithm itself.

This also fixes the file/class mismatch by renaming `strongly_connected_components.java` to `StronglyConnectedComponents.java`, and it makes the graph API safer by returning immutable adjacency/component views and enforcing bounds on edge input. Verification passed with `javac StronglyConnectedComponents.java` and `java -cp . StronglyConnectedComponents`.

